Greetings! 

Our team has some amazing news to share with you, today! Our game will be a part of this year's PAX East event, taking place March 21–24 in Boston! If you're there, be sure to visit our booth. 

And we're also ready to announce the game's full release date! 

Revival: Recolonization will be released as early as April 11! Keep the date on your calendar so you remember it.

[previewyoutube=AQngwLN8k2U;full][/previewyoutube]

In addition to this, we have prepared a new demo, which includes all the game's functionality and brand-new mechanics. The demo will be limited to 40 player turns, however, you can restart the demo as many times as you like to play 40 turns on a new game.

After the revolt of powerful artificial intelligence, the Earth was shaken by a terrible cataclysm, and human civilization collapsed overnight, sliding down to the primitive level of cavemen. But fragments of former greatness remain. Deep underground, the brilliant representatives of humanity – Emissaries – were waiting for their time to return, to rebuild cities, revive science and culture, and defeat the All-Mind. 

The demo will feature:

 Five Emissaries, each with their own specialities that affect their play style;
 Four epochs of development;
 Five tribes with different worldviews and gameplay peculiarities;
 Improved Edict system;
 Completely updated random event system – the consequences of choices now have a much greater impact on gameplay;
 New combat units: subs and aircraft carriers;
 A new dangerous automaton;
 Various options for diplomatic agreements;
 A map of Earth! 

A nice surprise for those who already have the game in their library: you can play the full version with all the changes through the closed beta before anyone else does. To access the beta build, simply: 

1. Click on Properties,
2. Then Betas,
3. Choose the available version and enter the password: revivalrelease

Take a stand against the All-Mind and restore the former greatness of mankind in the new Revival: Recolonization demo. Play, stream, and share your impressions of the game here or on Discord.

Regards,
Revival: Recolonization Team

Greetings, associate!

We are proud to release an update for Revival: Recolonization, which includes a number of bug fixes and gameplay tweaks. To access the latest build, please click on the "Download Demo" button on the game’s Steam page.

Please note — we will temporarily stop access to the Revival: Recolonization demo after 2-3 weeks. This will allow us to better process feedback and your suggestions.

Now, onto the full changelog!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/39245204/5b9f4f07e46a5df11ee75d85a2727484e110b670.jpg

Firstly, we have refined and tweaked the  tribes and clans system. Many of the changes made to the game are related to this system:

 updated the first contact and clan assimilation screens;
 added and recalculated bonuses from various tribe alignments, including combat;
 tweaked the cost of certain units; 
 changed descriptions and names for tribes and the pool of clan names (which is still WIP, so don’t be confused if you meet several duplicate clans on the game map belonging to the same tribe);
 added a UI window for selecting clan traits during assimilation;
 added game functionality/repercussions for a number of clan worldviews on the diplomacy screens, such as views on “mutations”.


{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/39245204/43827da4d118f68de4cfece7e595822230ebb97e.jpg

We have also implemented a ton of other fixes and updates to the game. The most notable ones are:

 limited the number of emissaries (factions) on the map to 7, with a unique colour for each;
 fixed a number of instances that lead to the game freezing;
 fixed issues during and after combat encounters that lead to unexpected results and occasional game freezes;
 fixed the English text on a few UI elements, descriptions and tips;
 fixed AI-related bugs, especially when the AI is attempting to assimilate clans; 
 tweaks were made to the resource economy;
 an automaton can no longer place an edict capsule in the city;
 dead/eradicated factions are no longer displayed in the “Society” window;
 minimum and maximum loyalty thresholds for assimilation changed to -10 \ +10;
 the "trade" worldview now tracks and depends on the number of active trade contracts, not the number of initiated ones;
 automatons no longer appear when assimilating tribes;
 when killing an automaton, a faction will now receive one of three rare resources: Electronics, Mutagen or Diamonds;
 ruins containing resources or a squad of automatons are more evenly distributed across regions;
 improved the algorithm for determining a good place to build a city;
 it is no no longer possible to attack a faction that was destroyed by the player, leave the poor sods alone!
 a faction’s city is now correctly displayed on the map after signing the appropriate agreement; 
 fixed a bug that occurred when the player was receiving an offer to sign a contract from the AI; 
 fixed a bug where the names of cities were visible in the fog of war;
 fixed a bug related to reputation count at the end of a turn.


{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/39245204/856092f2bf624854a14d4f8bf4dfaebc0e1e6159.jpg

Combat and equipment:

 added  swords, maces, and axes for melee units;
 gauss laser and cannon models for ranged units;
 added a long cannon for artillery (2nd epoch);
 added a large artillery tower (2nd epoch);
 4th epoch artillery units received a new animation and a singularity cannon;  
 1st epoch unit avatars now match their armour;
  lightsaber  colour effects added;
 when attacking with grenades, cover points are taken away;
 archers can no longer fight with axes, which is pretty logical, right?
 added a  galley (1st epoch ship);
 updated the model for the  “Walker” platform; 
 added a special ability called "Sacrifice a unit". Use with caution ;)
 the choice of several types of attacks simultaneously is now blocked;
 grenades no longer have the “Ground Attack” attribute associated with them; the attribute is now associated with shrapnel.

Visuals:

 updated the animation of the emissary's cloak;
 updated region colours on the strategic (diplomacy) map;
 a few icon-related fixes on the Science screen;

UI:

 redesigned the Resources window;
 unavailable equipment upgrades are now hidden from the player; 
 disabled fog of war on the strategic map;
 when trading relations are severed, the corresponding loyalty factor will decrease. Also, you cannot conclude a contract again while it is in effect.
 added a notification about some of the work-in-progress worldviews; 
 several sciences have been switched around on the Science Screen to make the research tree progression more logical;
 the shift button works again in the trade window, allowing you to add 10 units of goods per click.

We have also restored the compatibility of old save files. However, we still recommend you  start a new game  to experience all of the new features. We can't wait to hear your feedback on the new build!

Yours faithfully,
Revival: Recolonization Team

Greetings, associate!

Despite Revival being in Alpha and a lot of the systems still needing work, the response from players was enthusiastic so far! And our team is very grateful for that. 

Of course, a lot of aspects of the game need to improve before we can move to the next milestone and prepare Revival for an eventual release into Early Access. We plan to keep the Open Alpha running for the next 4 months at least and to make the overall game experience smoother, with your help and feedback. 

For now, enjoy the latest game patch that includes the following changes:

UI:

City and combat panels now remain correctly positioned within set boundaries;
Adjusted font size and text position within certain window borders;
Adjusted the size of a few UI elements, as well as their availability during opponent’s turn;
Outdated information removed from the unit panel;
All of the resources that are mined on a hex are now visible;
Resource icons removed from the strategic map;
Icon animation when zooming on the game map should be smoother now; 
Added tweaks to the diplomacy window between factions (emissaries);

Cities and Tribes:

When you take over another city, the surrounding fence is automatically rebuilt, as it should be;
Destroying automatons does not negatively affect your relationships with tribes; 
All the factors that influence tribe loyalty are now displayed correctly;
All tribe settlements now have a bonfire. They are two steps away from the invention of the wheel!
Fixed a bug with tribe assimilation, tribal warriors should now be available to the player;
Fixed a bug related to improving districts.

Combat system:

The unit panel in combat mode should now appear when clicked on;
When attacking a city, all participating units now correctly load into combat;
New types of icons for combat added;
Status "Hidden" is displayed for hidden units;
Merging with an army when leaving a city now works as it should;
Fixed a bug with certain weapons causing issues when used. 

Text and dialogue:

Corrected english translations of bits of text and dialogue;
Changed the wording of some of the notifications.  

Miscellaneous:

You can no longer buy a unit if you don't have enough money. Long live capitalism!
A foreign climate can no longer kill your units! Instead, their health drops to a critical level, but your troops and workers will stay alive;
Automatons no longer disappear near edict capsules. Now you will definitely have to fight them if you want to deactivate those capsules;
Fixed a few errors related to save files not loading correctly;
Fixed an error that occurred when crossing borders in an ocean.

This list was made to highlight some of the more noticeable changes in this update. The full list of changes is much longer, but we won’t bore you with that :) 

Update your game build via Steam and enjoy your time in the post-apocalyptic future. And of course, keep sharing your thoughts, ideas and stories with us! 

Respectfully,
Revival: Recolonization Team
